From c502b09a31e0cd1ae667a9d43d300ecdac62eb9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The browser Authors <noreply@browser.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:13:02 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/55] agent-fetch

Browser.agentFetch and agentFetchCancel: reads a URL the way a tab would,
in a page that is never shown and never appears as a target, renders and
settles HTML and extracts it as markdown in the renderer, or takes any
other response as it is before it commits; a method, header or body makes
the call a real fetch() from a document of the URL's origin. The widget
layer gains a headless native window so a headed browser can host the
off-screen page.

This commit owns the Browser-domain hub (browser_handler.*, Browser.pdl,
the chrome DevTools session and protocol config) and so also registers
recording and fingerprint-report; chrome/browser/devtools/BUILD.gn and
devtools_http_handler.cc hold their public state here, the production
commit adds its own hunks on top.
